## 1. Understanding What We Are Building

### 1.1 The Problem with the Current System (NetXMS)

When you asked the ATM department what they dislike, they said:
- **Misinformation** — the system shows wrong status
- **Information delays** — status updates arrive too late

This tells you exactly what "better" means to them. It is not about features. It is about **accuracy** and **speed**. Keep this in mind for every decision you make.

### 1.2 What We Are Updating vs What We Are Adding

**Updating (things we built but need to improve):**
- Database schema — needs vendor fields
- Simulators — NCR only, need GRG added
- Zabbix template — one template, need two
- Grafana dashboards — do not match NetXMS layout users know
- Report Portal — no EJ search

**Adding (things NetXMS has that we do not have yet):**
- State distribution donut chart (exactly like Image 1)
- Three-panel status layout (Out of Service / In Supervisor / Agent Disconnected)
- Fault distribution bar chart by fault type (Image 3)
- Per-ATM fault count table
- EJ search from main interface (not a separate Kibana URL)
- GRG vendor support throughout

### 1.3 The Two Vendors

| Vendor | Approx Count | Models | SNMP OIDs |
|--------|-------------|--------|-----------|
| NCR | 800-900 | SelfServ 34, SelfServ 84 | Custom NCR OID tree |
| GRG | 400-500 | BRM9, H22N | Custom GRG OID tree |

Everything in our system must handle both. The user should never need to know which vendor an ATM is — the system hides that complexity.

