## 6. Phase 5 — Fix the EJ Log Pipeline for Two Vendors

**Problem:** GRG logs use different field names than NCR. Elasticsearch receives both but Kibana search needs consistent fields.

### 6.1 Update Filebeat to Parse Both Formats

```bash
nano ~/projects/Dashen-Bank-ATM-monitoring-system/filebeat.yml
```

Replace the entire content with:

```yaml
filebeat.inputs:
  - type: log
    enabled: true
    paths:
      - /var/log/atm-ej/ATM-*.log   # NCR logs
    fields:
      vendor: NCR
      log_type: atm_ej
    fields_under_root: true
    tags: ["ncr", "atm-ej"]

  - type: log
    enabled: true
    paths:
      - /var/log/atm-ej/GRG-*.log   # GRG logs
    fields:
      vendor: GRG
      log_type: atm_ej
    fields_under_root: true
    tags: ["grg", "atm-ej"]

processors:
  # Extract ATM ID from the log line
  - dissect:
      tokenizer: "%{@timestamp} | %{atm_id} | %{terminal_id} | %{message_rest}"
      field: "message"
      target_prefix: ""
      ignore_failure: true

output.elasticsearch:
  hosts: ["elasticsearch:9200"]
  index: "atm-ej-live-%{+yyyy.MM.dd}"

setup.ilm.enabled: false
setup.template.name: "atm-ej-live"
setup.template.pattern: "atm-ej-live-*"
```

